UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The Five of Wands represents the absolute archetype of "Creative Friction"—the essential, high-entropy phase where multiple, competing trajectories, ideas, or individual wills collide within a shared operational space, forcing a rapid, evolutionary refinement of your strategy. Moving beyond the stability of the Four, the Five signifies the inevitable introduction of external volatility, which serves to stress-test your foundations and challenge the current limitations of your egoic architecture. Visually depicted as five figures engaged in a chaotic, non-lethal scramble with staves, this archetype embodies the concept of "Agile Iteration"—the understanding that progress is not a linear, solitary ascent, but a messy, multi-threaded process of negotiation, competition, and tactical adjustment. Within the complex architecture of your consciousness, this is the stage of "systemic turbulence," where the static of the status quo is disrupted by new input, forcing you to defend your position while simultaneously learning from the opposing vectors of others. When the Five of Wands appears, your system is registering a "Stress Test" status; the feedback loops you have established are being tested for bandwidth, speed, and resilience. This card commands you to abandon the desire for a controlled, static environment and instead embrace the volatility as a diagnostic tool: by observing how your energy interacts with the "noise" of the competition, you gain precise data on where your current model is rigid, where it is vulnerable, and where it requires greater, more adaptive sophistication. You are being tasked with the essential work of "dynamic positioning": navigating the conflict without becoming the conflict, maintaining your sovereign focus even as you engage in the necessary, ego-stripping work of refining your approach against the resistance of the manifest world. To inhabit the Five of Wands is to master the art of "creative warfare," understanding that true mastery is not the absence of opposition, but the ability to utilize that opposition as the friction required to sharpen your own, high-level intent, ultimately ensuring that the strongest, most resonant version of your vision is the one that survives the purge.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: When the Five of Wands appears in the reversed position, it acts as a high-intensity signal of "systemic avoidance," "internalized conflict," or the catastrophic breakdown of your ability to negotiate the necessary pressures of growth—a state where the external friction has been converted into a toxic, low-vibration state of psychological paralysis or destructive, misdirected aggression. The reversal suggests that instead of using the "chaos" of your current environment to iterate and refine, you are either retreating entirely from the field—withdrawing from competition to hide in a state of egoic fragility—or you are engaging in "shadow-boxing," where your vital energy is consumed by pointless, low-utility power struggles that have no connection to your actual, soul-level evolution. You are essentially "trapped in the noise," running a high-priority, high-cost maintenance script that prioritizes the avoidance of discomfort over the necessity of growth, leading to a profound, chronic state of agitation, unfocused reactivity, and a persistent, gnawing sense that you are losing your edge. From an analytical perspective, this is a clear sign that you are leaking your life force into a "feedback loop of defensiveness"; you are obsessively monitoring threats and reacting to every minor perturbation in your field, losing sight of the core, long-term trajectory you are meant to be pursuing. The reversed Five of Wands exposes the hidden, egoic fear that drives this behavior: the paralyzing terror of being truly seen in your imperfection, and the corresponding fear that if you were to engage honestly with the "competitors" or "critics" in your field, your fragile, constructed reality would be exposed as fraudulent. This reversal commands an immediate, radical intervention: you must stop the output of these avoidant, performative scripts, perform a brutal audit of your reaction protocols, and confront the reality of why you are so hesitant to stand in the arena and face the friction of reality. It is a demand to stop the self-deception that keeps you tethered to a state of chronic, high-maintenance reactivity, and to initiate the move toward a genuine, humble, and disciplined reclamation of your own, individual sovereignty. You are being tasked with the uncomfortable, yet essential, work of conflict integration—accepting that the "turbulence" you feel is not a failure of your strategy, but a necessary, high-value input that will allow you to evolve past your current, reactive ego-state and into a more powerful, resilient, and reality-aligned version of your soul’s manifestation.'
WHERE id = 19;
